# No `legacy-peer-deps` here any more, and it should not come back without a
# reason written down. It was covering for typescript-eslint@8 declaring
# `typescript@>=4.8.4 <6.1.0` as a peer while this project sat on TypeScript 7,
# which made strict peer resolution fail outright. That conflict is gone: the
# `typescript` slot is now an alias to `@typescript/typescript6`, which is the
# API the lint toolchain reads, and the TypeScript 7 compiler lives under
# `@typescript/native` where `npm run typecheck` calls it by name. Both are in
# devDependencies. `npm install` resolves cleanly with peers enforced.
